bevy-horizon: let NAK's unit tests build again on a PC

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 606441c9, after 0001-0015. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

mesa-switch comments out the #include <xf86drm.h> in nak_bindings.h (d4a00ea, "Merge
NaGaa95/mesa-switch main: Mesa 26.2.3, NVK and NAK fixes, shared shader cache"). Only
hw_runner.rs, which NAK's tests use to run shaders on a GPU, needs it, so the library still
builds, but NAK's test binary stops at 14 errors, the first "cannot find type drmDevicePtr".
The include is back behind __has_include: a PC build with libdrm compiles the tests again, and
the Switch build, whose image has no xf86drm.h, generates the same nak_bindings.rs as before.

With the whole series applied, NAK's tests build and pass on a PC (nak-host, Mesa's
builddir-test): 18 run, none fail, and the 53 in hw_tests:: and nvdisasm_tests:: are skipped,
as meson's test() skips them.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak_bindings.h b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak_bindings.h
index 7a77c4c..b2602b1 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak_bindings.h
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak_bindings.h
@@ -9,7 +9,10 @@
 #include "nouveau_context.h"
 #include "nouveau_device.h"
 
-// #include <xf86drm.h>
+#if __has_include(<xf86drm.h>)
+/* Only NAK's hardware tests use it, and the Switch has no libdrm. */
+#include <xf86drm.h>
+#endif
 #include "drm-uapi/nouveau_drm.h"
 
 #define DRM_RS_IOCTL(FOO) \
